* Sat May 23 2026 2.7.1-6
- Icons: hicolor-only apply (pack jolla/ scaled into hicolor; no live
  silica writes). Backup/restore snapshots hicolor + apk only.
- Icons: TPS basename matching for nativeMatchCount/apkMatchCount; drop
  2.4.3 desktop Icon= lookup and desktopfile helper.
- Icons: overlay uses packIconKeys / pack apk basenames for all packs;
  drop pack/type android special cases.
- docs/icons.md updated for the above.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.6.1-1
- Renamed the headless helper from sailfishos-uithemer-reassert to
  sailfishos-uithemer-icond. Boot unit is now
  sailfishos-uithemer-icond.service; themepacksupport-autoupdate.service
  and themepacksupport-systemupgrade.service ExecStart paths updated.
  Note: despite the -d suffix this is still a one-shot CLI; the actual
  long-lived privileged service remains /usr/libexec/sailfishos-uithemer
  -helperd over D-Bus.
- qmake: src/reassert/ replaced by src/icond/ (icond.pro, main source
  sailfishos-uithemer-icond.cpp).
- Spec: %post disables/removes the legacy reassert unit and stale binary
  before enabling the new service; %preun/%postun track icond and
  best-effort-clean the old unit name on uninstall.
- themepacksupport-systemupgrade.service: dropped ExecStartPost to the
  removed ocr_su.sh (leftover from the shell retirement).
- docs/icons.md and AboutPage updated to 2.6.1.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.6.0-1
- Architecture: GUI no longer runs as root. /usr/bin/sailfishos-uithemer
  drops its setuid bit (was 4755, now 0755) and removes setuid(0) from
  main(); it now runs as defaultuser like every other Silica app.
- New privileged D-Bus system service org.uithemer.UiThemer1, owned by
  /usr/libexec/sailfishos-uithemer-helperd (root, dbus-activated, 30s
  idle timeout). Three interfaces -- Themes (apply / restore / reassert
  / refresh-originals / theme-new-desktops / density-enable), Packs
  (uninstall), SystemServices (hide-icon / set-autoupdate /
  set-service-su / apply-hours) -- each gated by a polkit action,
  manage-themes / manage-packs / manage-system-services, all
  auth_admin_keep so the user is prompted once per ~5 minutes.
- New runtime dependencies: polkit, polkit-qt5-1.
- New build dependencies: pkgconfig(Qt5DBus), pkgconfig(polkit-qt5-1).
- Source layout: split into a subdirs qmake project. src/ops/
  (iconapplier, densityenabler, manifest, desktopfile, image util,
  file lock, spawner, themepack-ops) is shared via ops.pri by
  src/gui/, src/daemon/ and src/reassert/. FontApplier stays GUI-only
  because it is fully unprivileged once the GUI runs as defaultuser
  (writes ~/.config/fontconfig/conf.d, runs fc-cache as the current
  user).
- HelperClient (src/gui/helperclient.{h,cpp}, qmlRegisterType
  HelperClient): thin QDBusInterface-based proxy. Demuxes the
  daemon's per-interface OperationCompleted / Progress broadcasts
  into Qt signals matching the existing IconApplier /
  DensityEnabler / ThemePack / ThemePackModel surface so QML
  callbacks (onThemeApplied, onIconsRestored, onServiceChanged,
  onDpiRestored, onPackUninstalled, ...) keep working.
- ThemePack: privileged slots (hideIcon, enable/disable autoupdate,
  enable/disable servicesu, applyHours) forward to HelperClient and
  relay its signals; restartHomescreen drops scripts/homescreen.sh and
  becomes a single QProcess::startDetached("systemctl", "--user",
  "restart", "lipstick.service").
- ThemePackModel::ocr is now a pure GUI-side state machine: two
  daemon calls (SetAutoupdate(false), RestoreIcons) followed by three
  in-process steps (FontApplier::restoreFonts,
  DensityEnabler::restoreDensity(true,true), and dconf writes for
  /desktop/lipstick/sailfishos-uithemer/{activeIconPack,activeFontPack,
  autoUpdate}). No OneClickRestore D-Bus method.
- ThemePackModel::uninstall routes through Packs.UninstallPack(rpmName)
  and rebuilds the row list on the daemon's success broadcast.
- DensityEnabler: setuid(0) escalation in ensureEnabled() removed
  (only the daemon ever calls it, already root via systemd unit).
  restoreDensity drops the `su - defaultuser dconf` wrapper -- direct
  dconf calls work now that the GUI is defaultuser.
- FontApplier: chownToDefaultUser is gone (defaultuser already owns
  its $HOME). runFcCache drops `su - defaultuser` and runs fc-cache
  -f directly. confDir / confPath now derive from QStandardPaths so
  no more hard-coded /home/defaultuser/ assumption.
- src/ops/themepack-ops.{h,cpp}: extracted hideIcon, setAutoupdate,
  setServiceSu, applyHours bodies into a daemon-callable QObject
  matching the bash scripts they replace (timer unit text matches the
  retired apply_hours.sh case/esac verbatim).
- IconApplier stays a QML type for the read-only buildPreview /
  enableAutoTheming flows; QML's iconapplier.applyIcons /
  restoreIcons / reassertCurrentTheme calls migrate to helper.*.
  IconApplier::newDesktopsThemed signal in the GUI process triggers a
  helper.themeNewDesktops() round-trip when the watcher fires.
- DensityEnabler is no longer registered as a QML type; DensityPage's
  DensityEnabler { id: ... } block is removed, ensureEnabled is now
  helper.densityEnable(). The in-process restoreDensity instance
  stays as ThemePackModel::_density.
- /usr/bin/sailfishos-uithemer-reassert loses its setuid bit (was
  4755, now 0755). The 3 systemd units that drive it (themepacksupport
  -systemupgrade.service, themepacksupport-autoupdate.service,
  sailfishos-uithemer-reassert.service) already run as root by virtue
  of being system units, so the binary no longer needs the bit.
- spawner.h: setuid_ex macro removed.
- Spec: drop scripts/homescreen.sh, scripts/apply_hours.sh, tps/ocr.sh,
  tps/ocr_su.sh, tps/enable-autoupdate.sh, tps/disable-autoupdate.sh,
  tps/enable-servicesu.sh, tps/disable-servicesu.sh. %post tries
  reload dbus + reload polkit best-effort. %preun stops helperd and
  inlines the disable/stop systemctl calls the deleted
  disable-autoupdate.sh used to do. %postun reloads dbus + polkit.
- Legacy tps/ retired wholesale: deleted tps/themepacksupport.sh,
  tps/autoupdate-menu.sh, tps/systemupgrade-service.sh, tps/config.cfg,
  tps/config.shlib (and the now-empty scripts/, tps/ directories).
  Every privileged op the CLI used to drive lives behind the daemon's
  D-Bus interface. gui.pro drops the scripts/+tps/ INSTALL list; the
  spec drops `chmod +x %{_datadir}/%{name}/*.sh`, the `ln -sf
  themepacksupport.sh %{_bindir}/themepacksupport` symlink, the
  `%ghost %{_bindir}/themepacksupport` line, the harbour-
  themepacksupport backup/config.cfg migration block, and the matching
  `rm -f %{_bindir}/themepacksupport` from %postun. ThemePackOps
  loses the writeConfig() helper (no consumer survives); applyHours
  always daemon-reloads + restarts the timer instead of consulting
  config.cfg.
- Cover: CoverPage / CoverConfirm Connections target switches from
  iconapplier to helper (onIconsReasserted / onIconsRestored).
  CoverActionList1 / CoverActionList2 reassert paths call
  helper.reassertIcons() instead of iconapplier.reassertCurrentTheme().
- Version bumped to 2.6.0; AboutPage shows UI Themer 2.6.0.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.8-1
- Retired tps/install_dependencies.sh: it was a leftover from the
  removed graphic-theming / PNG-overwriting icon era (pkcon refresh +
  force-install all sailfish-content-graphics-default-z*-base and
  closed-z* packages). Current UI Themer does not touch those paths;
  the closed-* installs could also fail on community ports. Deleted
  the script; app.pro ships tps/* wholesale so it drops from the RPM.
- C++/QML: removed ThemePack::installDependencies() and the
  dependenciesInstalled() signal from ThemePack. WelcomePage.qml drops
  the entire Dependencies wizard block (Section, two Labels, install
  button, "I already installed" switch), the Connections handler that
  cleared settings.isRunning and published a notification on
  completion, and the unused vDep property plus BusyState /
  Notification imports and instances. Donate / Support section
  unchanged; "Start UI Themer" stays unconditionally enabled.
- Version bumped to 2.5.8; AboutPage shows UI Themer 2.5.8.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.7-1
- TPS: deleted four dead/quasi-dead artifacts under tps/:
  device-model (empty placeholder, retired in 2.5.5), size_droid and
  size_native (empty 0-byte placeholders, never read by anything in the
  workspace), and ddensity-menu.sh (only consumer was the now-trimmed
  D branch of themepacksupport.sh). app.pro ships tps/* wholesale so
  deleting from the workspace removes them from the package.
- TPS CLI: tps/themepacksupport.sh dropped the (F)ont theme and
  (D)isplay density menu lines and their F/f + D/d case branches.
  Both invocations dead-ended into deleted scripts (font-menu.sh was
  retired in 2.5.0, ddensity-menu.sh in this release), so the trim is
  cosmetic; the remaining branches (L/O/M/A/H/U/Q) are unchanged.
- Spec hygiene: %post no longer rm -f's device-model on upgrade. The
  2.5.5 cleanup has had a release cycle to clear pre-2.5.5 installs;
  size_droid / size_native get no cleanup either since they were
  always empty and harmless to leave behind on the rare upgrade.
- Version bumped to 2.5.7; AboutPage shows UI Themer 2.5.7.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.6-1
- icon_size_launcher: dropped the iconSizeLauncherSeed snapshot key.
  The "Restore display density" dialog now resets the live
  /desktop/sailfish/silica/icon_size_launcher key to the vendor default
  (Option B), matching how DPR is restored. DensityEnabler::ensureEnabled
  no longer captures or writes a seed; %post drops the legacy seed key
  via `dconf reset` on upgrade so it does not linger in user dconf.
- RestoreDDPage gains a second IconTextSwitch "Default icon size"
  (default checked) so the user can pick DPR-only, icon-size-only, or
  both. canAccept ORs the two switches.
- C++: new DensityEnabler::restoreDensity(bool dpr, bool iconSize) slot
  runs the dconf resets directly as defaultuser under FileLock, emits
  restored() unconditionally so the QML busy spinner drains. The seed
  helpers (kIconSizeSeedKey + read/writeDefaultUserDconf) were replaced
  by a single runDefaultUserDconf(cmd) wrapper.
- ThemePackModel::restoreDpi(bool, bool) forwards to
  DensityEnabler::restoreDensity via a one-shot signal connection. No
  more shell out; QML's onDpiRestored also rebinds cbiz.value so the
  ComboBox tracks the icon-size reset.
- Retired the restore shell trio: scripts/restore_dpi.sh,
  tps/restore_dpr.sh and tps/restore_iz.sh are deleted.
  ThemePack::restoreIZ (sole consumer of restore_iz.sh) is gone too.
  tps/ocr.sh and the spec %preun replace the deleted invocations with
  inline `su - defaultuser -c "dconf reset ..."` lines for DPR and
  icon size. %pretrans neutralisation list drops restore_dpr.sh /
  restore_iz.sh (no longer shipped, nothing to neutralise).
- Version bumped to 2.5.6; AboutPage shows UI Themer 2.5.6.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.5-1
- Device model: dropped the /usr/share/sailfishos-uithemer/device-model
  file end-to-end. %post no longer seeds it via `ssu mo`; the
  harbour-themepacksupport -> sailfishos-uithemer migration loop no
  longer carries it across; %post rm's any stale copy on upgrade.
- C++/QML: removed ThemePack::readDeviceModel(), Settings.qml's
  deviceModel switch, and Settings.qml's isXA2 helper (all hung off
  the device-model file). GuidePage.qml drops the XA2-specific
  "full restart may be needed" LabelText that depended on isXA2;
  the generic homescreen-restart hint above it is unchanged.
- TPS: deleted tps/apply_adpi.sh, tps/restore_adpi.sh, and the
  surviving tps/enable-dpi.sh (all relied on device-model and on
  Aliendalvik DPI plumbing that was removed in 2.5.4). Trimmed
  tps/ddensity-menu.sh down to the device pixel ratio + icon size
  branches and tps/ocr.sh to the still-meaningful steps (drop the
  font fontconfig conf inline + restore_dpr + restore_iz + dconf
  resets). The remaining bash entry points are still expected to
  go away when TPS is replaced wholesale by C++/QML.
- Spec hygiene: %pretrans neutralisation list drops restore_adpi.sh
  (no longer shipped). %preun no longer invokes the deleted
  restore_adpi.sh.
- scripts/restore_dpi.sh is now DPR-only: drops the second `adpi`
  argument and the /opt/alien -> restore_adpi.sh branch, matching
  ThemePackModel::restoreDpi(bool) which already passes a single
  flag.
- Version bumped to 2.5.5; AboutPage shows UI Themer 2.5.5.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.4-1
- Density: dropped the showDensity opt-in. The "Display density" pulley
  entry on MainPage and the D keyboard shortcut on every page are
  always available now (previously gated on a dconf bool that had no
  user-facing toggle anymore). GuidePage's density section is always
  visible; the XA2 LabelText keeps its hasAndroidSupport && isXA2 gate.
- Density: dropped the densityEnabled opt-in. Density customizations
  are always enabled. The user-facing "Enable display density settings"
  IconTextSwitch on DensityPage is gone, and the inner Grid is no
  longer gated. Settings.qml drops the densityEnabled property + alias;
  the legacy /desktop/lipstick/sailfishos-uithemer/densityEnabled key
  is left in dconf (harmless: nothing reads it anymore).
- Density: ported tps/enable-dpi.sh to a new C++ class DensityEnabler
  (src/densityenabler.{h,cpp}). ensureEnabled() is idempotent: it
  moves /etc/dconf/db/vendor.d/locks/{silica,ui}-configs.txt into
  /usr/share/sailfishos-uithemer/backup/dlocks/<name>.bk (skipping
  files already moved), runs `dconf update`, and snapshots
  defaultuser's /desktop/sailfish/silica/icon_size_launcher into
  /desktop/lipstick/sailfishos-uithemer/iconSizeLauncherSeed (only
  when the seed key is empty, never clobbers user-edited values).
  Serialises on the same FileLock sentinel as IconApplier /
  FontApplier. Called from DensityPage's Component.onCompleted so
  the lock-relocation self-heals on app open.
- Spec: %post mirrors DensityEnabler::ensureEnabled() inline so the
  bootstrap also runs on package install / upgrade. %preun replaces
  the disable-dpi.sh call with the inverse inline shell that puts
  the .bk locks back and refreshes dconf. tps/enable-dpi.sh and
  tps/disable-dpi.sh are removed from the source tree. The legacy
  $main/icon-z file produced by enable-dpi.sh is rm'd on upgrade
  (icon_size_launcher now lives in dconf instead).
- Spec hygiene: dropped disable-dpi.sh from the harbour-themepacksupport
  %pretrans neutralisation list (no longer shipped). Dropped the
  `touch -a droiddpi-current` from %post and droiddpi-current from
  the harbour-themepacksupport -> sailfishos-uithemer migration loop.
- Aliendalvik DPI: dropped the entire Android-DPI plumbing from the
  C++/QML surface. ThemePack loses droidDPI / getDroidDPI() /
  enableddensity() / disableddensity(); ThemePackModel loses
  applyADPI() and the adpi argument of restoreDpi(); DensityPage
  loses the Android DPI Slider Section and the XA2 LabelText;
  RestoreDDPage loses the "Default Android DPI" IconTextSwitch
  (canAccept now depends only on Default DPR) and the XA2
  LabelText. hasAndroidSupport stays since other consumers still
  rely on it. apply_adpi.sh / restore_adpi.sh remain on disk per
  the standing "TPS scripts are out of scope" rule and continue to
  back the legacy themepacksupport CLI; restore_dpi.sh is invoked
  with a single argument from C++.
- Note: tps/ocr.sh and tps/ddensity-menu.sh still reference the
  dropped enable-dpi.sh / disable-dpi.sh paths and write the legacy
  /desktop/lipstick/sailfishos-uithemer/densityEnabled key; per the
  standing TPS rule they will silently no-op until they are replaced.
- Version bumped to 2.5.4; AboutPage shows UI Themer 2.5.4.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.3-1
- Cover: removed the optional "Show active theme" switch from
  Options > Cover. The cover always shows the active icon / font
  labels now; per-row visibility is still tied to activeIconPack /
  activeFontPack not being default, so no rows appear when no theme
  is applied. Drops one indirection that hid the labels behind a
  dconf opt-in.
- Settings: dropped the coverActiveTheme dconf alias from
  qml/common/Settings.qml. The legacy key under
  /desktop/lipstick/sailfishos-uithemer/coverActiveTheme is left in
  the dconf db (harmless: nothing reads it anymore).
- Version bumped to 2.5.3; AboutPage shows UI Themer 2.5.3.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.2-1
- Cover: fix regression from 2.5.1 where icon and font active-theme rows
  disappeared entirely. Rows were gated on a non-empty
  readThemePackName(...) result; when /usr/share/harbour-themepack-<id>/package
  is missing or empty, that call returns "" and hid the whole CoverLabel
  (glyph + text). Visibility is again tied only to activeIconPack /
  activeFontPack not being default; the label prefers readThemePackName
  and falls back to a readable bare pack id (hyphens to spaces). Added
  shareDirPackId() so dconf values that already include the
  harbour-themepack- prefix are not doubled when opening package.
- Version bumped to 2.5.2; AboutPage shows UI Themer 2.5.2.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.1-1
- Cover: fix font CoverLabel being empty after applying / restoring /
  recovering a font theme. 2.5.0 made FontApplier synchronous, so the
  themeApplied / themeRestored / themeRecovered signals now fire
  inside the corresponding ThemePackModel call and clear
  settings.isRunning before the QML callback wrote settings.activeFontPack
  (or called settings.deactivateFont()). The cover therefore re-rendered
  the labels Column with a stale activeFontPack value. Reordered the
  dconf writes in qml/pages/MainPage.qml (apply + restore callbacks) and
  qml/pages/OptionsPage.qml (recovery callback) so they precede the
  C++ call. settings.activeIconPack / deactivateIcon() were reordered the
  same way for symmetry (icons apply is sync but does not clear
  isRunning, so the previous order was harmless there).
- Cover: tightened CoverPage.qml so the icon and font CoverLabel rows
  hide entirely when the resolved pack display name is empty, instead
  of showing a blank row with just the icon (covers the edge case
  where activeIconPack/activeFontPack is undefined or the pack's
  /usr/share/harbour-themepack-<pack>/package file is missing).
- Version bumped to 2.5.1; AboutPage label updated.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.5.0-1
- Font theming reimplemented in C++/QML on top of fontconfig:
  - New FontApplier class (src/fontapplier.{h,cpp}) writes a single
    per-user fontconfig conf file at
    /home/defaultuser/.config/fontconfig/conf.d/99-uithemer.conf that
    re-aliases `Sail Sans Pro Light` and `Sail Sans Pro` to the family
    exposed by the user-selected TTF inside
    /usr/share/harbour-themepack-<pack>/font/<weight>.ttf, then runs
    `fc-cache -f` as defaultuser. Restore = remove the conf file and
    refresh the cache. Recovery is identical to restore (nothing to
    reinstall: stock fonts under /usr/share/fonts are never modified).
  - Family name is read from the TTF via QRawFont so the alias matches
    Qt's lookup at runtime regardless of the file basename.
  - Non-latin packs: each `<pack>/font-nonlatin/<Lang>.ttf|.ttc` whose
    name is in the well-known set (Arabic, Devanagari, Chinese,
    Japanese, Hebrew, Thai) is added as a `lang`-tagged
    `<match target="pattern">` block so the right font is used per
    locale, instead of overwriting Jolla's DroidSans*.ttf.
  - Operations serialise on the same FileLock sentinel as IconApplier
    so font and icon jobs never race.
- ThemePackModel: applyTheme / restoreTheme / recoveryTheme now route
  through FontApplier instead of spawning bash. One-shot connections
  fire the corresponding themeApplied / themeRestored / themeRecovered
  signal exactly once per call (recovery does NOT also fire
  themeRestored, so MainPage's onThemeRestored handler does not run
  while OptionsPage is on top of the page stack).
- Aliendalvik (/opt/alien/system/fonts) font theming dropped: the
  Android runtime ignores fontconfig and we no longer overwrite stock
  files there.
- Removed shell scripts:
  - scripts/themeapply.sh
  - scripts/themerestore.sh
  - scripts/themerecovery.sh
  - tps/font-backup.sh
  - tps/font-restore.sh
  - tps/font-run.sh
  - tps/font-reinstall.sh
  - tps/font-menu.sh
  tps/themepacksupport.sh and tps/ocr.sh still reference some of these
  but the TPS interactive layer is going to be replaced separately and
  is left untouched here.
- RPM spec:
  - %preun: replaced the font-restore.sh call with an inline `rm` of
    the per-user fontconfig conf + `fc-cache -f` as defaultuser.
  - %post: dropped `touch -a font-current` and the corresponding
    migration entry; added cleanup of `font-current` and the legacy
    `backup/font*` directories on upgrade.
  - %pretrans: dropped `font-restore.sh` from the
    harbour-themepacksupport neutralisation loop (the file no longer
    exists on our side; the old TPS one is harmless).
- Version bumped to 2.5.0; AboutPage label updated.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.9-1
- Dialog layout: pulled `DialogHeader` out of the inner
  `SilicaFlickable` / `Column` and made it a direct child of the
  surrounding `Dialog` in ConfirmPage, RestorePage, RestoreDDPage
  and RecoveryPage. The flickable now anchors top to
  `header.bottom` and fills the rest of the dialog. This matches
  Silica's documented pattern and silences the
  `Cannot read property 'backIndicatorDown' / 'forwardIndicatorDown'
  of null` TypeErrors emitted from system DialogHeader.qml.
- Dialog header now sets `dialog: dlg...` explicitly so it never
  has to walk up through the flickable to find its owning Dialog.
- Removed the `backNavigation` / `forwardNavigation` /
  `showNavigationIndicator` bindings tied to `settings.isRunning`
  on the four dialogs above; toggling those handles while the
  header was alive was the trigger for the indicator-null binding
  evaluations. Interaction blocking during long-running operations
  is still enforced by the flickable's `enabled` / `opacity` and
  by `canAccept`.
- Version bumped to 2.4.9; AboutPage label updated.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.8-1
- Font preview: restore `font.weight` on the preview labels using a
  small QML helper that maps the selected font file basename (e.g.
  ibm-plex-Light, Regular) to `Font.Thin` … `Font.Black` via substring
  checks, with `Font.Normal` as fallback. This replaces the 2.4.7
  approach of leaving weight unset while still avoiding the old bug
  of binding a QString directly to `font.weight`.
- Version bumped to 2.4.8; AboutPage label updated.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.7-1
- Font preview: stop loading FontPreview / FontPreviewCover for
  themes that ship no fonts. The Confirm-page and cover-side
  Loaders are now `active: hasFont || hasFontNonLatin` with an
  empty initial source and a guard inside `reload()`, so an
  icon-only theme no longer triggers `<pack>/font/.ttf` lookups.
- Font preview: dropped the broken `font.weight: selectedFont`
  binding (it assigned a QString filename basename to an int
  enum slot, producing `Unable to assign QString to int` every
  time). The chosen weight is already encoded in the loaded TTF
  and rendered via `font.family: previewfont.name`.
- Font preview: gated `FontLoader.source` in both FontPreview.qml
  and FontPreviewCover.qml on non-empty `packName` and
  `selectedFont`, so a stray instantiation can never produce
  `<pack>/font/.ttf` paths.
- Cover page: gated `themepackmodel.readThemePackName(...)` in
  `CoverLabel.label:` bindings on a real, non-`default` active
  pack. QML evaluates `label:` even when the parent is
  `visible: false`, so without the guard an empty or `default`
  active pack triggered a read of `/usr/share/harbour-themepack-`
  / `/usr/share/harbour-themepack-default/package`.
- C++: `ThemePackModel::readThemePackName` now checks
  `QFile::open()` and returns an empty QString on failure,
  removing the underlying `QIODevice::read (QFile, ...): device
  not open` warning regardless of caller.
- Version bumped to 2.4.7; AboutPage label updated.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.6-1
- ConfirmPage / Cover icon-pack preview overhaul:
  - The preview is now built as a QImage in C++ and served from memory
    through a QQuickImageProvider registered under the "uithemer"
    scheme. QML reads it via `image://uithemer/preview/<packName>?t=<ts>`
    URLs (the `?t=...` query is an opaque cache buster). No PNG is
    written to disk anymore.
  - Fixed a long-standing bug where IconApplier::packDir would double
    up the "harbour-themepack-" prefix when the dialog passed the full
    list-name form (the previous on-disk PNG cache happened to mask
    this; the in-memory provider exposes it). packDir now strips the
    prefix if present so callers can pass either form.
  - Sampler now also walks `<pack>/jolla/`, matching the post-2.4.3
    native lookup that falls back to that subtree.
  - Fixed the "QML Column: Cannot specify ... centerIn anchors"
    warnings emitted while the dialog was open: the preview area is
    now an Item, the Image fills it with paddingMedium margins and
    only shows when status === Image.Ready.
  - Added a "No preview available" Label that takes over when the
    pack has no PNGs the sampler can find (Image.Error path).
- C++:
  - New IconPreviewCache (process-wide, mutex-guarded singleton mapping
    packName -> QImage) and IconPreviewProvider (QQuickImageProvider
    that strips the `?...` cache-buster query and the optional
    `preview/` segment, and honours requestedSize).
  - IconApplier::buildPreview now publishes the QImage to the cache
    and emits `previewReady(QString packName, bool ok)`; the on-disk
    `kPreviewPath` constant and the `mkpath(.../tmp)` call are gone.
  - The provider is registered on the QQuickView engine in main()
    before view->setSource so it is reachable by the time QML loads.
- RPM spec:
  - %post no longer creates `%{_datadir}/%{name}/tmp` and the
    harbour-themepacksupport migration loop no longer migrates the
    `tmp/` subdir.
  - One-shot %post cleanup removes any leftover
    `%{_datadir}/%{name}/tmp/iconspreview.png` and the (now unused)
    empty `tmp/` directory from older installs.
- Version bumped to 2.4.6; AboutPage label updated.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.5-1
- Removed the UI-mode tier system (`showGuimode` + `guimode` dconf keys):
  - Dropped the "UI mode" SectionHeader and the easy/full/advanced
    ComboBox from OptionsPage (and the side-effecting easy `onClicked`
    that disabled servicesu, the autoupdate timer, the second cover
    action and density). All settings are now always shown, including
    the former developer-only Icon updater (OptionsPage) and Backup &
    restore icons (GuidePage) sections.
  - Dropped `guimode` / `showGuimode` from Settings.qml (orphan dconf
    keys on existing devices are harmless).
  - Dropped the easy-mode-only "After confirming, your device will
    restart..." LabelText from ConfirmPage / RestorePage / RestoreDDPage
    and the redundant easy-mode overlay LabelText from ConfirmPage.
  - Keyboard handlers in MainPage / OptionsPage / AboutPage / GuidePage
    / TranslatorPage no longer gate Key_D / Key_W on `guimode`.
- Removed the "Custom build" feature:
  - Deleted docs/custom-build.md and the README "Custom builds" section.
  - Deleted scripts/sailfishos-uithemer.txt (the vendor dconf defaults
    file). %post no longer moves it into /etc/dconf/db/vendor.d/ and
    %preun no longer removes it. On upgrade, %post deletes any stale
    /etc/dconf/db/vendor.d/sailfishos-uithemer.txt left by older
    installs and refreshes the dconf db.
- Translations: dropped 8 now-orphan source strings (UI mode, easy,
  full, advanced, the three guimode descriptions, and "After
  confirming, your device will restart...") from every locale.
- Version bumped to 2.4.5; AboutPage label updated.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.4-1
- Removed sound theming (the Sailfish system sound theme that copied
  WAVs into /usr/share/sounds/jolla-ambient/stereo):
  - Dropped tps/sound-{run,restore,backup,menu,reinstall}.sh.
  - Removed the (S)ound theme entry from the CLI menu
    (tps/themepacksupport.sh).
  - One-click restore (tps/ocr.sh) no longer calls sound-restore.sh.
  - ConfirmPage / RestorePage / RecoveryPage no longer expose sound
    options; CoverPage no longer shows the active sound pack chip.
  - ThemePackModel slots applyTheme / restoreTheme / recoveryTheme
    no longer take a `sound` argument; hasSound() removed.
  - Settings.qml drops activeSoundPack (orphan dconf key on existing
    devices is harmless); scripts/sailfishos-uithemer.txt no longer
    seeds it.
  - On upgrade, %pretrans runs the still-on-disk sound-restore.sh once
    so the user's themed sounds are reverted to defaults BEFORE the
    new package wipes the script. %post then removes sound-current
    and backup/sound. Theme packs may still ship a `sound/` directory
    but it is silently ignored.
  - %pretrans no longer neutralises sound-restore.sh from older
    harbour-themepacksupport installs, %preun no longer invokes it.
  - Translations: dropped sound-only source strings; AboutPage and
    GuidePage / OptionsPage advanced-settings copy were rephrased to
    drop "sounds" and marked unfinished for translators.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.3-1
- Native icon lookup is now keyed off the .desktop's Icon= value (not its
  filename). This restores matches for built-in Jolla apps whose .desktop
  basename does not match the icon name, e.g. jolla-camera.desktop ships
  Icon=icon-launcher-camera, so a pack only needs icon-launcher-camera.png.
- Added pre-3.0 Jolla ambient subtree as a lookup-only fallback:
  <pack>/jolla/<zSize>/icons/<key>.png is consulted after native sizes for
  packs that still ship ambient artwork. PNGs under jolla/ are referenced
  via Icon= only, never copied into the system theme tree (graphic theming
  removal from 2.4.2 stays intact).
- nativeMatchCount, applyIcons and themeNewDesktops all read Icon= from
  the .desktop and pass it as the lookup key. APK lookup is unchanged.
- No system-tree writes; restore / reassert / manifest behaviour unchanged.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.2-1
- Removed graphic theming (the Sailfish system widget icons under
  /usr/share/themes/sailfish-default/silica/icons/):
  - Dropped tps/graphic-{run,restore,menu,backup}.sh.
  - Removed the (G)raphic theme entry from the CLI menu
    (tps/themepacksupport.sh).
  - One-click restore (tps/ocr.sh) no longer calls graphic-restore.sh.
  - %pretrans no longer neutralises graphic-restore.sh from older
    harbour-themepacksupport installs, %preun no longer invokes it,
    and %post no longer touches or migrates graphic-current.
  - Stale graphic-current state file (if any) is removed on upgrade.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.1-1
- Race fixes:
  - flock(2) on /usr/share/sailfishos-uithemer/icon-backup.lock serialises
    GUI apply / restore / reassert / refresh against the helper binary and
    the systemupgrade.service.
  - applyIcons commits each manifest entry BEFORE rewriting the .desktop
    file, so a crash mid-apply no longer poisons original_icon snapshots.
  - reassertCurrentTheme self-heals: snapshots a drifted Icon= as the new
    original before re-clobbering, and falls back to original_icon (and
    drops the entry) when themed_icon vanished.
- New auto-theming: QFileSystemWatcher on /usr/share/applications and
  /home/defaultuser/.local/share/applications themes any newly-installed
  app while a theme is active (no manual re-apply needed).
- Uninstalling the active icon pack now restores originals first so
  .desktop files do not end up pointing at a path that is about to vanish.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.4.0-1
- Icons applied by rewriting Icon= in .desktop files; no more PNG copies.
- Drop ImageMagick dependency; overlays and previews rendered with Qt.
- New JSON manifest /usr/share/sailfishos-uithemer/icon-backup.json tracks originals.
- New helper /usr/bin/sailfishos-uithemer-reassert (--reassert/--restore/--refresh-originals).
- New oneshot sailfishos-uithemer-reassert.service re-asserts the active theme at boot.
- systemupgrade.service now restores originals via the helper before system updates.
- autoupdate.service / timer driven by the helper; legacy run.sh becomes a thin shim.
- Drop Jolla ambient (z*), DynCal and DynClock support.
- Drop Tools backup/restore icons UI; covered by the manifest now.

* Sun May 10 2026 2.3.1-1
- APK launcher icons: /home/defaultuser/.local/share/apkd-bridge/launcherIcon (flat).
- Remove aliendalvik.service drop-in; APK refresh in autoupdate service/run.sh.

* Sat May 09 2026 2.3.0-1
- Merge Theme pack support engine into UI Themer; obsolete harbour-themepacksupport.
- Single install root under /usr/share/sailfishos-uithemer/; keep themepacksupport CLI.

